  "design_section": "7.13",
  "design_notes": [
    "The \"Twin / fact\" column is stored in twin. Commercial computer (single) shows none.",
    "Mass is tagged game_value: the design classifies only engine thrust and Isp as real-world approximate (7.0, 19) and says nothing about avionics mass.",
    "computer_count is not a table column. It is read from the option names: single = 1, \"three computers vote\" = 3, rad-hard + backup = 2, and plain radiation-hardened = 1 because the next row is the one that adds a backup.",
    "The table reliability is taken as the figure of the whole option. The redundancy formula of 6.5 does not reproduce it (three 97% computers in parallel give 99.997%, the table says 99.2%), so Core should not apply the formula on top of the table value. Open design question.",
    "radiation_bit_flip (8.4: \"Commercial computer, long mission\", mitigated by rad-hard or redundancy) is listed only for the single commercial computer. The design does not say how long a \"long mission\" is.",
    "software_overflow (8.4: \"Skipped software test\") is listed for every flight computer, with the software-in-the-loop test of 6.6 as its mitigation.",
    "\"Slow processor (guidance precision −10%)\" is a modifier on guidance_precision. Rad-hard + backup uses the same class of computer, but the design does not repeat the penalty there, so it carries none.",
    "\"More wiring & integration\" (triple-redundant) has no day or cost number; 6.7 says redundancy adds integration days without giving them. It is carried as a flag.",
    "No option is restricted to a contract. \"Best for crewed & deep space\" is advice, not a restriction."
  ],
